 "map_info": {
  "name": "Noise Layers: The Symphony of Frequencies",
  "title": "Coherent Noise Fundamentals",
  "lookup_name": "Noise_One",
  "description": "One sampled field, read twice on one bench: a ring that spends the field as relief beside a ring that spends the same field as colour, the same shader and the same noise scale on both. A marker stands on the same coordinate of each and the plate names that coordinate, the field's value there, and what each reading makes of it - including that the colour reading clamps the negative half of the field to black while the relief keeps it and pushes inward. FREEZE stops both of the shader's clocks (displacement offset and hue rotation), SAMPLE walks the marker round the ring, AMPLITUDE changes what the surface does with a value and FREQUENCY changes which value is at the coordinate at all. Nothing here carries a collider: the corrugation is in the vertex stage and cannot be touched. Corrected 2026-09-12: the previous description promised octave summation and a VR brush, neither of which this hall contains.",
